msgstr "数学基础"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:269
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Both implementations follow the `Flash-Attention 2` formulation of the "
"forward and backward passes: online softmax with a running max and sum in"
" the forward pass, and recomputation of `P` from `lse` with "
"{math}`\\Delta = \\mathrm{rowsum}(O \\circ dO)` in the backward pass. See"
" [Flash Attention 2 Math Derivation](./fa2_math_derivation.md) for the "
"full derivation that the kernels implement."
msgstr ""
"两套实现都遵循 `Flash-Attention 2` 的前向与反向公式：前向使用维护 running max 与 running sum 的 "
"online softmax，反向利用 `lse` 重算 `P`，并使用 {math}`\\Delta = \\mathrm{rowsum}(O "
"\\circ dO)`。kernel 所实现的完整推导请参见 [Flash Attention 2 "
"数学推导](./fa2_math_derivation.md)。"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:271
msgid "Learnable Attention Sink"
msgstr "可学习 Attention Sink"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:273
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The sink only affects the softmax denominator, so neither implementation "
"touches the mainloop for it. On SM90, the sink LSE is merged into `lse` "
"and `O` is rescaled in the forward postprocess kernel, and `dsink` is "
"computed in the backward preprocess kernel. On SM100, the direct-store "
"path passes {math}`\\mathrm{logsumexp}(\\mathrm{sink})` to the kernel as "
"one extra logit per head, the locked-merge path folds it in the forward "
"postprocess kernel, and `dsink` comes from a separate kernel in which the"
" last CTA of each head reduces the partial sums in a fixed order. See "
"[Support Learnable Attention Sink](./attn_sink.md) for the math and the "
"distributed implementation."
msgstr ""
"sink 只影响 softmax 的分母，因此两套实现都无需为它改动主循环。在 SM90 上，前向 postprocess kernel 把 "
"sink 的 LSE 合并进 `lse` 并重缩放 `O`，`dsink` 则在反向 preprocess kernel 中计算。在 SM100 "
"上，直接写回路径把 {math}`\\mathrm{logsumexp}(\\mathrm{sink})` 作为每个 head 额外的一个 "
"logit 传给 kernel，加锁合并路径则在前向 postprocess kernel 中将其折叠进来；`dsink` 由一个独立 "
"kernel 计算，每个 head 的最后一个 CTA 按固定顺序归约各部分和。数学推导与分布式实现见 [Support Learnable "
"Attention Sink](./attn_sink.md)。"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:275
msgid "Muon QK-Clip"
msgstr "Muon QK-Clip"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:277
msgid ""
"`return_max_logits=True` returns the maximum attention logit per head. On"
" SM90, each CTA reduces row maxima into a shared-memory slot per head "
"with an atomic max and then updates global memory with another atomic "
"max, so `num_heads_q <= 128` is required. On SM100, conditional rescaling"
" means the running max lags the true max, so the softmax warpgroups track"
" an exact row max in a separate register. The global update uses an IEEE "
"bit-pattern trick: a signed integer max for non-negative values and an "
"unsigned integer min for negative values. See [Support Muon QK-"
"Clip](./muon_qk_clip.md) for the distributed reduction across CP ranks "
"and stages."
msgstr ""
"`return_max_logits=True` 会返回每个 head 的最大 attention logit。在 SM90 上，每个 CTA "
"先用原子 max 把各行最大值归约到 shared memory 中每个 head 的槽位，再用一次原子 max 更新 global "
"memory，因此要求 `num_heads_q <= 128`。在 SM100 上，由于条件重缩放会让 running max "
"滞后于真实最大值，softmax warpgroup 会在单独的寄存器中记录精确的行最大值；全局更新利用了 IEEE "
"位模式技巧：非负值用有符号整数 max，负值用无符号整数 min。跨 CP rank 与跨 stage 的分布式归约见 [Support Muon"
" QK-Clip](./muon_qk_clip.md)。"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:279
msgid "Sparse Attention"
msgstr "稀疏注意力"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:281
msgid ""
"On SM90, sparse attention runs inside the same kernel family. "
"`BlockSparse` expresses uniformly sized key blocks through ranges, "
"`IndexSparse` reads a `(total_q, num_heads_kv, topk)` index tensor "
"directly, and the producer gathers K/V rows with `cp.async` (or TMA when "
"key blocks are at least 128 tokens). The backward pass picks `LoopK` when"
" key blocks are small. On SM100, `IndexSparse` has dedicated forward and "
"backward kernels built around `PackGQA` tiles of 128 rows with shared "
"token-level indices, together with a top-`k` kernel. These kernels are "
"standalone and not yet wired into the distributed path. See [Optimize "
"Sparse Attention in FFA](./sparse_attn.md) for the design and benchmarks."
msgstr ""
"在 SM90 上，稀疏注意力运行在同一个 kernel 家族中：`BlockSparse` 通过 ranges 表达大小统一的 key "
"block，`IndexSparse` 直接读取形状为 `(total_q, num_heads_kv, topk)` "
"的索引张量，producer 用 `cp.async`（key block 不小于 128 个 token 时用 TMA）gather K/V "
"行；key block 较小时，反向选用 `LoopK`。在 SM100 上，`IndexSparse` 有专门的前向与反向 "
"kernel，围绕共享 token 级索引的 128 行 `PackGQA` tile 设计，并配有一个 top-`k` kernel。这些 "
"kernel 目前是独立的，尚未接入分布式路径。设计与 benchmark 见 [Optimize Sparse Attention in "
"FFA](./sparse_attn.md)。"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:283
msgid "FFA_FA4 Backend"
msgstr "FFA_FA4 Backend"

#: ../../source/blog/native_ffa.md:285
msgid ""
"`FFA_FA4` is a temporary Blackwell backend built on a forked `Flash-"
"Attention 4` with an `HSTU Function` mask representation. It is not part "
"of the native `FFA` kernel and is never selected by default. It is "
"described in [Support Blackwell with FFA_FA4 "
"Backend](./blackwell_ffa_fa4.md)."
msgstr ""
"`FFA_FA4` 是一个临时的 Blackwell backend，基于 fork 的 `Flash-Attention 4` 并使用 "
"`HSTU Function` mask 表示。它不属于原生 `FFA` kernel，也永远不会被默认选中。详见 [Support "
"Blackwell with FFA_FA4 Backend](./blackwell_ffa_fa4.md)。"

